<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mireya Moscoso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mireya Moscoso is a Panamanian politician who was president of Panama from 1999 to 2004, the country's first woman president. The widow of the three-times president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulfo-arias">Arnulfo Arias</a>, she led his Arnulfista Party and presided over the transfer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> on 31 December 1999. Her government was later criticised for corruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mireya-moscoso.jpg" alt="Mireya Moscoso" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Embassy of United States in Panama · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mireya_Moscoso_in_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
